.\" Man page for rhc-heartbeat.
.TH HEARTBEAT 1 "2026" "rhc-heartbeat" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
heartbeat \- collect and report system heartbeat data

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B heartbeat \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIFLAGS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B heartbeat
is a service for collecting and reporting system heartbeat data.
It periodically collects a heartbeat describing the system, caches any
records that could not be delivered, and uploads them to the configured
Prometheus endpoint using the system's RHSM identity certificate.
.P
Only one instance may run at a time; a lock file prevents concurrent runs.
Pending heartbeats that failed to upload are retained and retried on the next
run. A pending cache that cannot be read is rotated aside: the broken file is
renamed with a Unix timestamp suffix and left in place for investigation,
and the run continues with a fresh cache.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Collect and upload a heartbeat. Failed uploads keep the record in the pending
cache for a later retry.
.TP
.B config
Print the resolved configuration as JSON to standard output.
.TP
.B profile
Collect a heartbeat and print it as JSON to standard output.

.SH FILES

.TP
.I /etc/rhc/rhc-heartbeat.conf
Main configuration.

.TP
.I /etc/rhc/rhc-heartbeat.conf.d/
Drop-in directory; TOML files here override values from the main
configuration.

.SH EXAMPLES

.TP
Collect and upload a periodic heartbeat:
.B /usr/libexec/rhc/heartbeat run

.TP
Inspect the resolved configuration:
.B /usr/libexec/rhc/heartbeat config

.TP
Inspect a collected heartbeat without uploading it:
.B /usr/libexec/rhc/heartbeat profile

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B heartbeat
is intended to be a zero-config program that does not require user input.
The following override variables should only be used during development.

.TP
.B RHC_HEARTBEAT_CONFIG=/etc/rhc/rhc-heartbeat.conf
Path to the configuration file.

.TP
.B RHC_HEARTBEAT_DROPINS=/etc/rhc/rhc-heartbeat.conf.d/
Directory with configuration drop-ins overriding the main configuration.

.TP
.B RHC_HEARTBEAT_RHSM_CONFIG=/etc/rhsm/rhsm.conf
Path to the subscription-manager configuration.

.TP
.B RHC_HEARTBEAT_SYSPURPOSE_FILE=/etc/rhsm/syspurpose/syspurpose.json
Path to the subscription-manager system purpose cache.

.TP
.B RHC_HEARTBEAT_PENDING_CACHE=/var/lib/rhc/heartbeat.jsonl
Path to the pending heartbeat cache.

.TP
.B RHC_HEARTBEAT_LOCK=/run/rhc-heartbeat/heartbeat.lock
Path to the lock file.

.TP
.B RHC_HEARTBEAT_CONSUMER_CERT|KEY=/etc/pki/consumer/cert|key.pem
Paths to the consumer identity used for TLS client authentication.

.TP
.B RHC_HEARTBEAT_PRODUCT_DIR=/etc/pki/product|product-default
Directories with installed product certificates.
